<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Berlin Declaration (1945)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1945</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> Declaration of 5 June 1945 was issued by the four Allied commanders, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwight-d-eisenhower">Eisenhower</a>, Zhukov, Montgomery and de Lattre de Tassigny, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s unconditional surrender. It stated that no central German government remained and that the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, the United Kingdom and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> assumed supreme authority over Germany. It provided the legal basis for the Allied occupation and the Allied Control Council.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/berlin-declaration-1945.jpg" alt="Berlin Declaration (1945)" width="320" height="265" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: US Army · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:US_Army_Germany_occupation_zones_1945.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
